 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of voxels, multiplied by a constant factor for the number of faces (6) and vertices per face (6). Specifically, $36 \times N$ vertices are processed [S4, S5, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for storing the voxel data and temporary geometry buffers.
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of voxels, multiplied by a constant factor for the number of faces (6) and vertices per face (6) [S4, unofficial][S5, unofficial]. Specifically, $36 \times N$ vertices are processed [S4, unofficial][S5, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for storing the voxel data and temporary geometry buffers [S5, unofficial][S8, unofficial].
 *   **Performance:** Extremely inefficient for large volumes. A $128 \times 32 \times 32$ chunk generates 786,432 draw calls if not instanced [S4, unofficial]. Performance degrades rapidly due to CPU-GPU overhead of uploading and drawing $36 \times N$ vertices every frame [S5, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths:** Simple to implement; no complex meshing algorithms required; easy to debug individual voxels [S5, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** High draw call overhead; no face culling between adjacent voxels (every voxel draws all 6 faces unless explicitly checked); lighting and other visual effects are harder to implement compared to other voxel rendering techniques [S2, S5, unofficial].
-*   **When not to use:** Large-scale voxel engines or real-time applications requiring high frame rates [S4, S7, unofficial].
